    "final_answer": "I have successfully retrieved the information about a pre-trained model optimized for question answering on Hugging Face. Here's the comprehensive answer:\n\n## Example Pre-trained Model for Question Answering on Hugging Face\n\n**Model**: `deepset/roberta-base-squad2`\n\n### Model Details:\n- **Type**: Pre-trained model based on `roberta-base`, fine-tuned on the SQuAD 2.0 dataset\n- **Task**: Extractive Question Answering (QA)\n- **Architecture**: RoBERTa-based Transformer model\n- **Training Data**: SQuAD 2.0 (Stanford Question Answering Dataset)\n- **Eval Data**: SQuAD 2.0 validation set\n- **License**: cc-by-4.0\n- **Popularity**: ~522,886 downloads last month\n- **Hardware Used**: 4x Tesla V100 GPUs\n\n### Languages Supported:\n- **English only** 🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿\n\nThe model was trained on SQuAD 2.0, which is an English-only dataset, so it is specifically optimized for English-language question answering tasks. The model card explicitly lists \"Language: English\" in its overview section.\n\n### Evaluation Results:\n- **Exact Match** on SQuAD v2 validation: 79.931\n- **F1 score** on SQuAD v2 validation: 82.950\n\n### How it Works:\nThis model was designed for extractive QA, meaning it finds the span of text in a provided context that best answers a given question. It was trained on the SQuAD 2.0 dataset which includes both answerable and unanswerable questions, making it robust at detecting when a question cannot be answered from the given context.",
